Z||000000||JohnnyK||10-19-2000||10:35 PM||||Well, I'm sure it was running rich, and the plugs (especially number 4) are covered with black stuff, and the engine is out, so anyone have any idea what it could be? I'm thinking I could get to the problem more easy with the engine out, except I can't really start the engine. It burns oil SOMETIMES. If I am having a hard time starting it, it will burn oil, but if not, it won't. (Usually have a hard time starting). I can start it by cranking for about 8 seconds, but then it will die, unless I hold down the gas, and then it revs really, really, rough while chugging out black smoke. But sometimes it doesn't.. Ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FieroGTRacingInc||10-20-2000||12:01 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">...   It's probably your timing, But I had the same type problem and I got responses of.......  stuck or broke injector(s),MAP sensor,timing,ign. module.....  I just changed my MAP and kept play with my timing and went through 3 set's of plug's.....  and yes I even changed the front three all 3 times... and  I really don't know...  It finally started.   This did'nt help you at all....  sorry  ||||reg||1
Z||000002||WisconsinGT||10-20-2000||12:41 AM||||Johnny, sounds like your #4 cylinder has had it's better days. I would do a compression test. Might be time for a rebuild.||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnnyK||10-20-2000||01:29 PM||||Well, I was going to sell it in the spring. I will do the compression test, as I meant to get around to it, but never did. Also, I think I do need timing... Thanks guys!||||reg||1
